Hookflow depends on, and its Docker images / Helm chart pull in, a number of
third-party open-source components under their own licenses. A generated,
versioned inventory of every direct and transitive dependency and its license
is committed at docs/licenses/ (see docs/licenses/README.md) and regenerated
in CI (`.github/workflows/license-report.yml`) so it never drifts silently
out of date with the poms/package.json/composer.json it was built from.

Notable licenses among bundled/runtime components, called out here because
they are not MIT/Apache-2.0/BSD/ISC (the common case for the rest of the
stack — see the full report for the complete list):

